e E1 |\n| E26 | `tree_add_node` | `has_root != 0` and `parent_id` not in the map | `stderr: \"Error: Parent node %lu not found\\n\"`, returns `-1`, node freed | [x] |\n| E27 | `tree_add_node` | parent already has `child_count >= MAX_CHILDREN` (32) | `stderr: \"Error: Parent has maximum children\\n\"`, returns `-1`, node freed | [x] |\n| E28 | `tree_add_node` | `hashmap_put` fails | `stderr: \"Error: Failed to add node to hashmap\\n\"`, returns `-1`; the id **stays** in the parent's `child_ids` | [x] unreachable through the ABI (needs a `calloc` failure); guard translated verbatim |\n| E29 | `tree_remove_node` | `tree == NULL` | returns `-1`, no output | [x] |\n| E30 | `tree_remove_node` | `id` not in the tree | `stderr: \"Error: Node %lu not found\\n\"`, returns `-1` | [x] |\n| E31 | `tree_remove_node` | same `id` removed twice | second call: `stderr: \"Error: Node %lu not found\\n\"`, `-1` | [x] |\n| E32 | `tree_remove_node` | `id` whose parent is no longer in the map (parent lookup returns NULL) | parent-unlink step skipped, subtree still removed, returns `0` | [x] |\n| E33 | `tree_remove_subtree` (static) | node id not found | returns `-1` (observable: `node_count` not decremented) | [x] |\n| E34 | `tree_get_node` | `tree == NULL` | returns `NULL` | [x] |\n| E35 | `tree_get_node` | `id` absent | returns `NULL` | [x] |\n| E36 | `tree_contains` | `tree == NULL` / absent `id` | returns `0` | [x] |\n| E37 | `tree_size` | `tree == NULL` | returns `0` | [x] |\n| E38 | `tree_print` | `tree == NULL` | prints `\"(empty tree)\\n\"` | [x] |\n| E39 | `tree_print` | `tree->has_root == 0` (fresh tree, or root removed) | prints `\"(empty tree)\\n\"` | [x] |\n| E40 | `tree_print_helper` (static) | `root_id` not in the map (`has_root != 0` but node gone) | prints nothing at all | [x] |\n| E41 | `tree_get_depth` | `tree == NULL`, or `id` not contained | returns `-1` | [x] |\n| E42 | `tree_get_height` | `tree == NULL`, or `id` not contained | returns `-1` | [x] |\n| E43 | `tree_count_descendants` | `tree == NULL`, or `id` not contained | returns `-1` | [x] |\n| E44 | `tree_find_path` | `tree == NULL`, or `path == NULL`, or `id` not contained | returns `-1`, `path` untouched | [x] |\n| E45 | `tree_find_path` | `max_length` smaller than the real path length — `max_length = len-1`, `1`, `0`, `-1`, `INT_MIN` | returns `max_length` (**including negative values**), writes exactly `max(max_length, 0)` entries | [x] |\n| E46 | `main.c` `assert(...)` (86 assertions in 14 test functions) | any library result differing from the expected value | `stderr: \"driver: <file>:<line>: <func>: Assertion \\`expr' failed.\"` + `SIGABRT` | [x] all 14 exported `test_*` functions run in a forked child; exit status + both streams compared |\n\n## Boundary/robustness cases also covered (generic ABI boundaries)\n\n| # | case | note | [x] |\n|---|------|------|-----|\n| B1 | NULL for every pointer parameter of all 20 library entry points | `hashmap_{put,get,remove,contains,size,clear,destroy}`, `tree_{delete,add_node,remove_node,get_node,contains,size,print,get_depth,get_height,count_descendants,find_path}` + `path == NULL` + `data == NULL` | [x] |\n| B2 | `tree_id_t` extremes | `0`, `1`, `u64::MAX`, `u64::MAX-1`, `1<<63`, ids that collide in the same bucket | [x] |\n| B3 | `int` extremes across the FFI boundary | `max_length` = `i32::MIN`, `-1`, `0`, `1`, `i32::MAX` | [x] |\n| B4 | oversized `data` | 255, 256, 257, 300, 1024-byte C strings → truncation to 255 chars + NUL | [x] |\n| B5 | zero-length `data` | `\"\"` and `NULL` (only `data[0]` initialised — the rest of `data` stays uninitialised in **both** implementations, so only the NUL-terminated prefix is compared) | [x] |\n| B6 | non-ASCII / high-bit `data` bytes | bytes `0x80..0xFF`, invalid UTF-8 — must round-trip verbatim through `printf(\"%s\")` | [x] |\n| B7 | out-of-range enum values | the C API declares **no** `enum` and no flag/mode parameter; the only non-pointer, non-integer-range inputs are `tree_id_t` (full `u64` range, all valid) and `int max_length` (full `int` range, covered by B3). Nothing to reject. | n/a |\n\n## Documented C undefined behaviour — deliberately not exercised\n\nThese are *not* rejections; the C code has no guard and would crash or read\nout of bounds. A differential test would only compare two crashes, so they are\nlisted for completeness instead:\n\n* `hashmap_put/get/remove` with a hand-built `hashmap_t` whose `capacity == 0`\n  → `hash % 0` (SIGFPE in C, panic in Rust).\n* `hashmap_*` / `tree_*` with a non-NULL but invalid (dangling) pointer.\n* `tree_delete` with `tree->node_map == NULL`, or `tree_*` on a `tree_t` whose\n  `node_map` is invalid.\n* A hand-built `tree_node_t` with `child_count > MAX_CHILDREN` → reads past\n  `child_ids` in C.\n* Use-after-`tree_delete` / use-after-`hashmap_destroy`.\n* A parent chain that does not reach `root_id` (`tree_get_depth`,\n  `tree_find_path` would loop; `tree_find_path` is capped at 1000, so it is\n  reachable only by mutating `parent_id` by hand).\n"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":421,"cache_read_input_tokens":116455,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":421,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9135168b-ddb2-4629-80cd-b34a9b6f8618","uuid":"a55f58b4-2415-45f2-88cf-a2cc27304c05","timestamp":"2026-08-19T20:49:21.956Z"}
