{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_3yhannwmbw6luajjypreswyjgzaej3enuzadpin2q5pe3pez24iq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification is complete. Here's the summary.\n\n## What I found first (the blocking issue)\n\nThe existing Rust \"translation\" had **no C-ABI surface at all**: no `#[no_mangle]`, a generic `Hashmap<V: Copy>` with `Option<V>` values, a `Vec` arena instead of `malloc`'d nodes, and struct layouts incompatible with `hashmap.h`/`tree.h`. `main.c`'s 14 non-`static` `test_*` functions and `main` existed only as private functions inside the binary. So **0 of the C library's 35 symbols were exported** and nothing could be verified through the FFI boundary.\n\n## What I changed (Phase A completeness work)\n\n- **`src/hashmap.rs`, `src/tree.rs`** — rewritten as faithful pointer translations: `#[repr(C)]` structs verified against the C compiler's `sizeof`/`offsetof` (24/32/536/32 bytes), `libc::malloc/calloc/free`, byte-order-faithful FNV-1a, and `#[no_mangle] extern \"C\"` on all 20 public functions. Fields the C leaves uninitialised (`child_ids`, `data[1..]` when `data == NULL`) are left uninitialised.\n- **`src/driver.rs` + `src/lib.rs`** — `main.c` translated and exported (14 `test_*` + `main`); `src/main.rs` stays a thin bin whose output is byte-identical to `c_src/build/driver` (1499 B stdout, 72 B stderr).\n- **`src/cio.rs`** — output goes through the *same* `FILE *stdout/stderr` as `printf`, so buffering and bytes match.\n- **Counters** → `wrapping_add/sub`: C wraps `size_t`; Rust debug builds panicked (rows E48/E49 now prove `SIZE_MAX` parity).\n\n## Artifacts\n\n| file | content |\n|---|---|\n| `SYMBOLS.md` | all 35 `nm -D` symbols, **35/35 exported by Rust, 0 missing, 0 extra**, 0 non-libc undefined + mutation-sensitivity table |\n| `ERRORS.md` | 49 rejection rows (E1–E49) + 7 generic-boundary rows + documented-UB list |\n| `CONFIGS.md` | 36 valid-config rows (C1–C36) + feature-combination table |\n\n## Results (all via `libloading` on both `.so`s, never calling Rust directly)\n\n```\nPhase B  32 rows  0 failed   78,313 comparisons\nPhase C  54 rows  0 failed    2,763 comparisons\nPhase D   5 rows  0 failed       24 comparisons\n```\nPassing under `--no-default-features`, default, `--all-features` (the crate declares no `[features]`, so that is the complete set) and in **both debug and release**.\n\nTwo bugs in my own verification, worth flagging:\n1. **`cargo test` does not rebuild a `cdylib` no test links against.** Every comparison was silently running against a stale `.so` — caught only because a deliberately mutated hash constant went *undetected*. Fixed with an `rlib` dependency edge plus a freshness guard in `rust_so_path()`.\n2. My C4 expectation was wrong (resize happens on the **14th** insert, since `12/16 == 0.75` is not `> 0.75`) — the C is correct; I corrected the test and `CONFIGS.md`.\n\nSensitivity was then proven by injecting 11 single-line defects (hash prime, `>` → `>=`, dropped `deleted_count++`, clamped negative `max_length`, `strncpy` off-by-one, missing root `parent_id = 0`, `height` without `+1`, a missing space in `printf`, a removed `#[no_mangle]`, non-wrapping counters) — **all 11 were caught**. Allocation-failure branches (E1/E2/E5/E21/E25) are genuinely exercised via an `LD_PRELOAD` injector, and probe-exhaustion/orphan-parent branches via hand-built (public) structs. Nothing in `c_src/` was modified."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1038,"cache_read_input_tokens":284539,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1038,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9135168b-ddb2-4629-80cd-b34a9b6f8618","uuid":"c312c32c-f240-452d-9fce-927f3265069a","timestamp":"2026-08-19T21:14:05.654Z"}
